# Line endings are NOT normalised by Git in this repository - they are already LF
# on disk and stay LF everywhere. Same reasoning as rtlsdrPager/.gitattributes,
# but with the opposite starting point.
#
# Git for Windows sets core.autocrlf=true by default, which would rewrite every text
# file to CRLF on checkout. Two things break if that happens:
#
#   - rtl-sdr/ and libusb-andro/ are vendored from osmocom/rtl-sdr, rtlsdrblog/rtl-sdr-blog
#     and libusb, all of which store LF. PROVENANCE.md promises the files are byte-identical
#     to upstream apart from the documented patches. A CRLF checkout turns "diff against a
#     fresh upstream clone" into thousands of whitespace hits and hides the real ones.
#   - the tree has to build on Linux and CI too.
#
# `-text` means: store the bytes as they are, hand them back as they are.
* -text
